This directory vendors five files from the official CLEGR benchmark
repository:

  https://github.com/rethinking-graph-language-evals/CLEGR

  (arXiv 2508.20583, "A Graph Talks, But Who's Listening? Rethinking
  Evaluations for Graph-Language Models", NeurIPS 2025 New Perspectives on
  Graph Machine Learning workshop)

Vendored files (from src/data/gqa/ upstream), unmodified except as noted:
  - types_.py
  - functional.py
  - questions.py
  - generate_graph.py   (one dependency patch: `import bezier` and its one
                          call site replaced with an equivalent pure-numpy
                          cubic Bezier evaluation, since the `bezier` PyPI
                          package ships no wheels for Python 3.13+ and fails
                          to build from source in this project's
                          environment -- see `_cubic_bezier_evaluate_multi`
                          in the file for the exact substitution. No other
                          logic was changed.)
  - args.py

